AgentOps stands for Agent Operations.

It is a platform used to monitor, debug, and evaluate AI agents while they are running.

Think of it like a dashboard for AI agents.

Instead of watching servers, it watches what AI agents are doing.

Without AgentOps
User
   │
   ▼
Agent 1
   │
   ▼
Agent 2
   │
   ▼
Result

If something goes wrong, it's difficult to know:

Which agent failed?
Which prompt caused the issue?
How long each agent took?
How many LLM calls were made?
With AgentOps
             AgentOps Dashboard
                    ▲
                    │
User → Agent 1 → Agent 2 → Result
        │           │
        └───────────┘

AgentOps records what each agent is doing.

What AgentOps can monitor
✅ Which agent started first
✅ Which agent finished
✅ Execution time
✅ LLM prompts
✅ LLM responses
✅ Errors and exceptions
✅ Token usage
✅ Cost estimation
✅ Performance metrics

